1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,600
Last year, scammers took 913 million
dollars from people in Singapore.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:09,000
In four out of five cases, the victim
pressed send themselves.

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:17,400
To the bank, those payments look normal:
the right phone, the right password,

4
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:19,000
the right one-time code.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,600
The evidence is in the conversation that
persuaded them, and banks never see it.

6
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,400
PauseGuard checks the conversation, not
just the transaction.

7
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:32,000
This is the live prototype, running on
Google Cloud.

8
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,800
Mrs Tan is 67.

9
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:43,600
A man claiming to be from MAS tells her to
move her savings to a safe account.

10
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:47,600
When she sends eight thousand dollars to a
new account,

11
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:52,800
PauseGuard asks her one simple question:
who asked you to make this payment?

12
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,400
She shares the chat.

13
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,400
Gemini agents read her screenshot,

14
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:01,600
while the payee and the scammer's number
are checked against the bank's watchlist.

15
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:04,800
In about ten seconds, the payment is held.

16
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:09,200
She sees exactly why, on her own
screenshot, in plain words,

17
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:13,600
with a button to call her son and the
anti-scam helpline.

18
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,400
At the bank,

19
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:36,200
the case reached the analyst console
before Mrs Tan's screen even changed,

20
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:37,800
through Firestore's realtime listener.

21
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:43,000
Gemini has written the case file: the
evidence with the red flags boxed,

22
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,200
her 90-day history with this transfer
standing out,

23
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:49,000
and web intel grounded in Google Search.

24
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,600
One key reports the scam, and the
scammer's number,

25
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,800
account and link are blocked for every
customer.

26
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,000
Not every case needs a hard stop.

27
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Raj is told to top up four hundred and
fifty dollars to unlock his commission.

28
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,400
PauseGuard explains the pay-to-earn job
scam and suggests a 24-hour pause.

29
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,000
Raj stays in control.

30
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:25,000
And it stays out of the way.

31
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,600
Aisyah is paying a deposit to her new
landlord and attaches the tenancy
agreement.

32
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:35,400
Gemini reads the PDF, finds nothing
suspicious, and the payment goes through.

33
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:45,000
Under the hood: the app is on Firebase
Hosting with Firebase Auth.

34
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:49,800
Five ADK agents run on Cloud Run, with
Gemini on Vertex AI.

35
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:53,400
Firestore stores the cases and powers the
live console,

36
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:55,400
and BigQuery scores transaction risk.

37
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:59,800
The verdict itself comes from plain,
tested rules, so it's auditable.

38
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:07,400
On a hundred held-out test cases, rules
alone stopped 78 percent of scams.

39
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:11,800
PauseGuard stopped all of them, with a 4
percent false-positive rate,

40
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:14,200
for under a cent per check.

41
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,200
Fraud models check the transaction.

42
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:20,800
PauseGuard checks the conversation.

43
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:24,400
Try it live at pauseguard-sg dot web dot
app.
